    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="tc-overview">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="tc-overview" data-i18n="ovTitle">01 · Overview</h2>
      <div class="chapter-body pair">
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovProbT">The problem</h3>
          <p data-i18n="tcProb">
            TentosCap, the financial arm of 3tentos, lent farmers money for their crops, repaid at harvest in
            soybean sacks. Knowing how much they owed in sacks meant checking the day’s soybean price, asking a
            TentosCap representative and doing the math.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovGoalT">The goal</h3>
          <p data-i18n="tcGoal">
            Design TentosCap’s first credit card app end to end: a no-annual-fee Visa with limits set by an in-app
            credit analysis and a balance paid in full at the end of the harvest, ready for a public launch at
            CropShow on February 28, 2023.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="tc-field">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="tc-field" data-i18n="tcFieldTitle">02 · Field Observations</h2>
      <figure class="chapter-body quote">
        <p class="quote-lead" data-i18n="tcQuote">
          At launch, most farmers cared more about getting through onboarding quickly than about security.
        </p>
        <figcaption data-i18n="tcQuoteCap">
          Informal interviews at the CropShow launch, Santa Bárbara do Sul
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="insights three">
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="tcO1t">Skeptical by default, yet excited at the promise</p>
          <p data-i18n="tcO1">
            As with anything new, many farmers met the card with skepticism at first, but some were excited about
            a card whose payments follow their harvest cycle.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="tcO2t">Speed over security</p>
          <p data-i18n="tcO2">
            Most farmers cared more about how fast they could finish onboarding and request the card than how the
            processes would work.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="tcO3t">Hands-on onboarding</p>
          <p data-i18n="tcO3">I guided farm-operation leads through onboarding myself during the event.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

